From 860bc6db0fcbd9c8d6c1ed1deb9c09a6aa85d365 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antigravity <antigravity@gemini.local>
Date: Wed, 30 Jul 2026 12:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/pm: let GFXCLK ceiling float in PROFILE_PEAK on SMU14

On SMU14 parts (RDNA4 / gfx1200 / gfx1201),
smu_v14_0_set_performance_level() programs GFXCLK's soft max in
PROFILE_PEAK the same way it does for every other force level: a
fixed value taken from the DPM table's peak entry (~2.0 GHz).
Because SetSoftMaxByFreq pins the ceiling to that exact frequency,
PMFW's opportunistic boost logic can never raise GFXCLK above it,
even though the ASIC is capable of boosting past 3.0 GHz under
favorable power/thermal conditions.

PROFILE_PEAK is meant to request maximum performance, not clamp it,
so GFXCLK's upper bound should be left to float (firmware-managed,
0xffff) rather than pinned, while its floor still gets pushed up to
the peak DPM level to bias the firmware toward high clocks.

Fix this by, for PROFILE_PEAK only, issuing an extra
smu_v14_0_set_soft_freq_limited_range() call that sets just the
floating max (min=0 so only the max-side message is sent), then
letting the existing call set just the floor (max=0 so only the
min-side message is sent). Every other force level takes the
original single-call path unchanged, and no other clock domain
(MCLK, SOCCLK, VCLK, DCLK, FCLK) or the function's public signature
is touched.

Signed-off-by: Antigravity <antigravity@gemini.local>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu14/smu_v14_0.c | 23 ++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu14/smu_v14_0.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu14/smu_v14_0.c
@@ -1268,10 +1268,28 @@ int smu_v14_0_set_performance_level(struct smu_context *smu,
 	}

 	if (sclk_min && sclk_max) {
+		bool sclk_max_auto = (level == AMD_DPM_FORCED_LEVEL_PROFILE_PEAK);
+
+		if (sclk_max_auto) {
+			/*
+			 * Let GFXCLK's ceiling float to the firmware-managed
+			 * boost limit instead of pinning it to the DPM
+			 * table's peak entry, so PROFILE_PEAK can reach full
+			 * hardware boost clocks.
+			 */
+			ret = smu_v14_0_set_soft_freq_limited_range(smu,
+								    SMU_GFXCLK,
+								    0,
+								    sclk_max,
+								    true);
+			if (ret)
+				return ret;
+		}
+
 		ret = smu_v14_0_set_soft_freq_limited_range(smu,
 							    SMU_GFXCLK,
 							    sclk_min,
-							    sclk_max,
+							    sclk_max_auto ? 0 : sclk_max,
 							    auto_level);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
